        "observation_dependencies": [
          "qpos",
          "qvel",
          "tcp_pose",
          "red_pose",
          "blue_pose",
          "red_goal",
          "blue_goal"
        ],
        "output_semantics": "Each prediction slot represents its Cartesian command at that slot's pre-action time and contains [3 anchor-relative TCP position metres, 6 world TCP rotation columns, 1 native gripper scalar, 4 anchor scores]. Anchor score argmax selects red object, blue object, observed red destination, or observed blue destination. Training positions are relative to the selected anchor in that slot's pre-action observation; decoding resolves that anchor from the freshly measured current observation, adds the learned displacement, projects the 6D orientation by Gram-Schmidt, and invokes panda_kinematics.solve_ik from fresh measured joints. Object anchors cover approaches and the temporary red transfer; destination anchors cover transport/placement after lift. Gripper >=0 opens and <0 closes under the common executor. Prediction slots are t-1 through t+14 and host execution uses slots 1 through 8 starting at current t.",
        "parameter_semantics": "There are no caller parameters: call_args is always the empty object. Intent is fixed to the complete buffer-swap task. Inputs use measured Panda joints in radians, velocities in radians/s (finger channels in metres and metres/s), and world-frame TCP, block and observed goal poses in metres with wxyz quaternions. Every demonstration is bound once with call_args={}; the model must infer progress from causal physical state.",
